From 9efea697e29c7309f283d5bd908c7dc0bdeadc05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:43:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] fix(proton): install the ARMv8.0 build when the
 installed release was changed by component updates

A Snapdragon 685's log: droiddeck-proton-armv80 copied the installed DroidDeck-Proton 11-12.8 (2 GB,
32 s) and then stopped on "files/lib/wine/vkd3d-proton/aarch64-windows/d3d12.dll is not the file the patch
was made for", at every start, so the ARMv8.0 build was never installed. DroidDeck's component updates
keep that release's DXVK, vkd3d-proton and FEX DLLs current, so its files are no longer the release's.

- The files the component manager swaps are checked before the copy; any other changed file is caught
  while patching. Either way the verified release is downloaded (resuming, once) and used instead, and a
  changed base is remembered so it is not copied again after a failed download. The user's own tool is
  never modified.
- ComponentsManager.protons() leaves out the ARMv8.0 build (.droiddeck-armv80): a swapped-in or updated
  DXVK, vkd3d-proton or FEX build would bring the LSE atomics back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
